            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Italian for the junction, then the Italian for to overtake."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: accelerare",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "accelerare — \"to speed up, to accelerate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Non accelerare, c'è la nebbia. Do not speed up, it is foggy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "L'acceleratore is the accelerator pedal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "accelerare is a learned borrowing from Latin accelerāre 'to hasten' (EtymDB), built on celer 'swift'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
